& [Purpose]
  + provide the smallest read-only official-SDK inspection seam for caller-launched ephemeral sessions; not a full autonomous agent or installation

& [SJSProcessing]
  + delineate raw semantic wire from MCP transport bookkeeping native stdio duplication and caller application custody
  + refine byte correspondence separately from semantic truth executable identity installed acceptance and model quality
  + reapply bounded session and no ambient pathname provider remote or service effects
  + prune dispatch forks generic launchers provider adapters durable custody app edits and unbounded default SDK read_until
  + seven-fold exhaustion selects one tool fixed bounds existing codec and explicit native runtime shutdown rather than a general service
  + data design retains original nested wire JSON and fixed faults while identifying aggregate output as reservation not delivery

& [Requirements]
  + [CIMA-001] preserve attributed source lineage current Pinky authority isolated D checkout and protected foreign C narrative
  + [CIMA-002] add one safe-Rust cantor_sop_inspect_mcp workspace crate and zero-argument native executable using installed official rmcp3.0.1 without changing the pinned wire stdio semantics consumer or golden fixtures
  + [CIMA-003] expose only inspect_sop_semantics with exactly one SDK-normalized wire_request_json String argument; retain nested raw bytes and do not claim duplicate MCP-envelope detection
  + [CIMA-004] bound decoded raw wire request at262144 bytes before strict original parsing and complete wire response at1048576 bytes before export
  + [CIMA-005] delegate semantic inspection to unchanged deterministic wire response production and preserve exact original response JSON string rather than parse/reserialize its bytes
  + [CIMA-006] define strict versioned typed reply with inspection_succeeded semantic_refused adapter_refused byte counts SHA256 optional exact response fixed fault code and explicit non-authority
  + [CIMA-007] export structuredContent with fixed text summary and is_error true for semantic or adapter refusal; unknown tool uses official method-not-found
  + [CIMA-008] declare tools-only readonly non-destructive idempotent closed-world metadata with no resources roots sampling provider model or command tools
  + [CIMA-009] retain official SDK protocol codec compatibility including BOM notifications and complete-value EOF; use SDK Transport not a forked parser
  + [CIMA-010] limit MCP input frame2097152 bytes output frame4194304 bytes aggregate actual input8388608 bytes plus one overflow witness and aggregate reserved output8388608 bytes
  + [CIMA-011] admit at most32 decoded messages including initialization notifications and one active semantic call; busy refusal does not create a product queue
  + [CIMA-012] cancel the SDK session on codec budget output or handshake fault without reporting reserved output as delivered bytes
  + [CIMA-013] bound whole native session60 seconds and explicit runtime shutdown wait250 milliseconds using two async workers and at most two blocking stdio workers
  + [CIMA-014] safely duplicate only already-inherited stdio handles or descriptors into path-free File wrappers; do not acquire filesystem paths arbitrary handles listeners subprocesses storage or services
  + [CIMA-015] reject extra CLI arguments and session faults with exit2 and fixed non-echoing cantor_semantic_inspection_mcp_refused newline; initialized normal disconnect exits0
  + [CIMA-016] distinguish generic caller-owned I/O timeout from native process termination and document ephemeral session restart ownership rather than indefinite resident-agent availability
  + [CIMA-017] map all eight existing golden cases directly with five exact complete wire responses and three adapter outer refusals; do not issue the different EOF ConsumerReceipt
  + [CIMA-018] prove official SDK client initialize list call Unicode empty pagination semantic refusal unknown-tool and malformed-wire recovery
  + [CIMA-019] test argument shape strict nested wire bytes exact/plus-one size busy response limit frame aggregate reservation message and pending-I/O deadline adversaries
  + [CIMA-020] prove fresh native process no semantic custody carry CLI malformed oversized input closed output and actual withheld-input/unread-output deadline exit using bounded developer capture kill/reap fallback
  + [CIMA-021] statically audit prohibited ambient effects and retain unchanged predecessor hashes explicit stdio exception and no Linux runtime claim without measured gates
  + [CIMA-022] retain physical component formation and implementation manifests actual focused debug/overflow-release results complete workspace gates Clippy warnings-denied format and evidence replay
  + [CIMA-023] bind requirement-by-requirement completion proof review exact per-element graph artifact identities narrative source and procedural signature before completion publication
  + [CIMA-024] publish only attributable owned paths plus justified transitive manifests with non-force push direct origin equality immediate bookend and no foreign/provider/remote/application writes

& [AcceptanceGates]
  + [CIMA-A01] five exact wire outputs and three distinct adapter refusals replay deterministically
  + [CIMA-A02] official SDK client and native sessions obey bounded transport deadline and fixed public fault
  + [CIMA-A03] every unsupported argument byte frame budget and concurrency adversary fails closed
  + [CIMA-A04] pinned predecessors remain unchanged and no ungranted ambient effects appear
  + [CIMA-A05] actual focused and full current-tree gates physical evidence and requirement matrix support all twenty-four requirements
  + [CIMA-A06] signed owned implementation is non-force published and immediately bookended without installed-agent claims

& [NonAuthority]
  + no provider model network listener pathname acquisition persistent storage arbitrary handle process shell service installation update remote message app edit merge or operator approval
  + semantic reply is not a ConsumerReceipt and SDK-normalized arguments cannot prove rejected duplicate envelope keys
  + procedural signature is not cryptographic operator approval; no Linux or installed consumer acceptance claim

& [State]
